> > If given Magicbane, pull it from the bag and switch to it once you have
> > the Amulet to absorb curses.
>
> Hmm... You give the bow a high priority, as I see. Maybe I should
> enhance bow next. I already have a dozen elven daggers at basic.

For classes that can multifire daggers, daggers beat any other
missile.  For classes that can multifire arrows but never daggers
that preference can reverse.  Caveman is limited to basic in
dagger so never gets multifire.  At skilled in bow multifire is very
limited but does happen.

The game never gives monsters both daggers and bows, so when
the monster attack code process it throws/fires anything it has
as it advances then switches to melee face to face.  It is clear
that using missiles is good strategy, but *which* type of missile
to use when several are available is a matter of comparing skills,
figuring out the price in ?oEW and so on.

When you enchant a stack of a dozen elven daggers, that's a
price that lasts the whole game.  Same with a bow.  But *not*
the same with a stack of arrows.

